# Every text file here is stored with LF endings and is checked out that way on
# every platform. Git for Windows otherwise checks the tree out with CRLF, since
# core.autocrlf defaults to true there, while the MSYS2 git that the build calls
# has it off: every file then looks modified, and the version string that comes
# from "git describe --dirty" ends up marked dirty. Keeping LF also means the
# shell scripts under packaging/ stay runnable under MSYS2.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Content that must never be touched, whatever the heuristics decide.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
